{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet85rkDgttzrfM6ow6WM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough understanding. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`Order.kt`**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values, and add `status: OrderStatus` field to the `Order` data class.\n\n2. **`OrderController.kt`**: \n   - Update `create()` to initialize new orders with `status = OrderStatus.ACTIVE`\n   - Add new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n     - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n     - Returns 200 OK with the cancelled order if order is already CANCELLED\n     - Returns 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (changes nothing)\n     - Otherwise, sets order to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns 200 OK with cancelled order\n\n3. **`ShipmentRepository.kt`**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order.\n\n4. **`ShipmentController.kt`**: Update `create()` to check if the order is CANCELLED and reject with 409 if so.\n\n5. **`ApiError.kt`**: Add two new error codes: `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (409 when cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipments) and `ORDER_CANCELLED` (409 when creating shipment for CANCELLED order).\n\n6. **`OrderControllerTest.kt`**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order successfully\n   - Cancel already cancelled order (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment (conflict, nothing changes)\n   - Cancel non-existent order (404)\n\n7. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**: Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order (409).\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could have put cancel logic in a separate OrderService class, but existing controllers directly use repositories and have business logic, so consistency requires keeping logic in controller\n- Could use database constraints instead of application-level checks, but this is an in-memory repository demonstration\n- Could have used Optional<Order> instead of null checks, but existing code uses null and throws exceptions\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel active order | Order, all shipments by orderId | Order status→CANCELLED, CREATED shipments→CANCELLED | 200 + Order | return from endpoint |\n| Cancel already-cancelled order | Order | nothing | 200 + Order | return from endpoint (idempotent) |\n| Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment | Order, shipments | nothing | 409 Conflict | throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED) |\n| Cancel non-existent order | nothing | nothing | 404 Not Found | throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) |\n| Create shipment for cancelled order | Order, Shipment | nothing | 409 Conflict | throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `OrderControllerTest.`\n   - `cancel_active_order_succeeds()` - create active order, cancel it, verify status=CANCELLED in response\n   - `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds()` - create order, cancel twice, second cancel returns 200 (idempotent)\n   - `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409()` - create order, create shipment, confirm it, attempt cancel returns 409, verify order still ACTIVE and shipment still CONFIRMED\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404()` - attempt to cancel unknown order, verify 404 and error code\n\n2. `OrderControllerTest.` (for shipment cancellation):\n   - `cancel_order_cancels_created_shipments()` - create order with CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify shipment status becomes CANCELLED\n\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.`\n   - `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409()` - cancel order first, attempt to create shipment, verify 409 and error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1635,"cache_read_input_tokens":20180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1635},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82238496-2cee-4019-8ddd-ee18987bd2ed","uuid":"216ce011-ae59-4313-94ae-ea8c14ca9990","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:44:28.028Z","request_id":"req_011Cet85qzZmKbqkaRBTTeD3"}
