{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet8E4Yqe5RcnWkG9D2pJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All 20 tests passed with 0 failures. The command was `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` and the result shows:\n\n- Tests run: 20\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- BUILD SUCCESS\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - `./mvnw test` completed successfully with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All original tests in OrderControllerTest, ShipmentControllerTest, CustomerControllerTest passed (existing tests not broken)\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint** - Added in OrderController with proper behavior:\n   - Cancels active orders (OrderControllerTest line: `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_returns_cancelled_order`)\n   - Persists cancelled status (verified in test assertions)\n   - Cancels CREATED shipments (OrderControllerTest line: `cancel_order_cancels_all_created_shipments`)\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent** - Uses existing ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException with new ErrorCode entries\n5. ✅ **Edge cases covered**:\n   - Repeated cancel succeeds (OrderControllerTest: `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotent`)\n   - Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing (OrderControllerTest: `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing`)\n   - Unknown order rejected with 404 (OrderControllerTest: `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404`)\n   - Shipment creation for cancelled order rejected with 409 (ShipmentControllerTest: `rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_error_envelope`)\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** - Only modified Java/Kotlin source and test files\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified necessary files in order, shipment, and api packages\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status: OrderStatus` field to Order. Necessary because orders now have lifecycle states.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Updated `create()` to initialize status=ACTIVE; added `cancel()` endpoint that:\n   - Validates order exists (404 if not)\n   - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments (409 if any exist, with no changes)\n   - Sets order to CANCELLED and cancels CREATED shipments atomically\n   - Idempotently handles already-cancelled orders\n   Necessary for the cancel requirement.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order. Necessary for cancel operation to find related shipments.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Updated `create()` to check if target order is CANCELLED and reject with 409. Necessary to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes. Necessary for error responses.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 8 new tests covering all cancel scenarios. Necessary to verify implementation.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 1 new test for shipment creation on cancelled order. Necessary to verify constraint.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All ticket requirements have been implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders atomically, idempotently handles retries, rejects if any shipment is confirmed, rejects unknown orders, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order (required for order lifecycle)\n- OrderController.kt: Updated create() to initialize ACTIVE status and added cancel() endpoint (required for cancellation logic)\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method (required to find shipments for cancellation)\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders (required for constraint)\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes (required for error responses)\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 8 tests for cancel functionality covering all cases (required for verification)\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment creation on cancelled order (required for verification)\n\nTests:\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_returns_cancelled_order` - Verifies active orders can be cancelled and status changes to CANCELLED\n- `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds` - Verifies idempotency of cancel operation\n- `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - Verifies 404 for unknown orders\n- `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` - Verifies atomicity: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, nothing changes and 409 is returned\n- `cancel_order_cancels_all_created_shipments` - Verifies all CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n- `newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status` - Verifies new orders initialize with ACTIVE status\n- `rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_error_envelope` - Verifies 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory executed successfully. Result: 20 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nNot done: Nothing. All acceptance criteria have been met and verified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3340,"cache_read_input_tokens":34723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3340},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82238496-2cee-4019-8ddd-ee18987bd2ed","uuid":"95b07693-fd71-4df8-b406-7eea45348bf0","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:46:17.186Z","request_id":"req_011Cet8E3mxNimeUBy4nwQNp"}
